{"event_index": 9, "event": "proposal_response", "at_utc": "2026-11-05T05:36:33.157255+00:00", "candidate_id": "c0001", "stage": "init_01", "generation": 0, "generation_order": 1, "prompt": "Solving a black-box graph combinatorial optimization problem via stochastic solution sampling following \"heuristics\".\nThe `heuristics` function takes as input a matrix of edge attributes with shape `(n_edges, n_attributes)`, where `n_attributes=1` in this case. It computes prior indicators of how promising it is to include each edge in a solution. The return is of the shape of `(n_edges,)`.\nFunction interface: def heuristics_v2(edge_attr: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\nPropose a new heuristic without an existing heuristic.\nReturn exactly <thought>algorithm description</thought> followed by <code>the complete executable Python module, including import numpy as np and def heuristics_v2(edge_attr: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:</code>. Do not use tools or read files. No other text or Markdown fences.", "response": "<thought>For each edge, compute a robust low-cost desirability score by combining its inverse empirical percentile with a sigmoid of its robustly standardized value. Lower edge attributes receive larger indicators. The rank component remains stable under arbitrary scaling, while the robust sigmoid preserves stronger distinctions near the center and limits the influence of outliers. Constant or non-finite inputs are handled safely.</thought><code>import numpy as np\n\ndef heuristics_v2(edge_attr: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = np.asarray(edge_attr, dtype=float)\n\n    if x.ndim != 2 or x.shape[1] != 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"edge_attr must have shape (n_edges, 1)\")\n\n    n_edges = x.shape[0]\n    if n_edges == 0:\n        return np.empty(0, dtype=float)\n\n    values = x[:, 0]\n    finite = np.isfinite(values)\n\n    if not np.any(finite):\n        return np.full(n_edges, 0.5, dtype=float)\n\n    valid = values[finite]\n    median = np.median(valid)\n    mad = np.median(np.abs(valid - median))\n    scale = 1.4826 * mad\n\n    if scale <= np.finfo(float).eps:\n        scale = np.std(valid)\n    if scale <= np.finfo(float).eps:\n        scale = 1.0\n\n    standardized = np.zeros(n_edges, dtype=float)\n    standardized[finite] = (values[finite] - median) / scale\n    standardized = np.clip(standardized, -12.0, 12.0)\n\n    order = np.argsort(np.where(finite, values, np.inf), kind=\"mergesort\")\n    ranks = np.empty(n_edges, dtype=float)\n    ranks[order] = np.arange(n_edges, dtype=float)\n\n    valid_count = np.count_nonzero(finite)\n    if valid_count > 1:\n        percentile = 1.0 - ranks / (valid_count - 1.0)\n    else:\n        percentile = np.full(n_edges, 0.5, dtype=float)\n\n    sigmoid = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(standardized))\n    score = 0.6 * percentile + 0.4 * sigmoid\n\n    score[~finite] = 0.0\n    return np.clip(score, 0.0, 1.0)</code>"}
